From 22d3d6bdd34b27704db62b3bcf7f29a932ffd3ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:58:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Emitter round-3 repairs: positive-tape bridges, the 4A
 mapping rewritten

Repairs both round-2 majors and the minor. The bridge contracts now
require 0 < C.k, closing the zero-tape degeneracy under which
stateWord 0 identifies all arguments and the install conclusion was
satisfiable for an arbitrary noncomputable function; the docstrings
record the auditor's witness and why the clause is load-bearing.
Design section 11c supersedes 11b item 3 in full: the parser-validation
framing is withdrawn (every binary word is a legitimate Cook-Levin
source instance; the auditor's empty-language witness is recorded) and
replaced by the real stage-to-seam mapping -- silent preparation packs
the inherited s1-s5 records into the loop's initial state word, then
one family member per round over the fixed family order with
R = n+(k+3)T+k+1, positive-duration empty rounds, the terminator on
the last chunk, and the exact serialization ledger. Section 11a
carries the supersession marker the auditor requested.

Verification: combined fresh 57/57 sweep (with the A-continuation
integration), zero error lines, 20 admissions; the full-print closure
regression passes; Build lint unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
